  "reason": "The strongest completed result is config_018 (multimodal, multiprofile, PCA, ResNet50, avgpool, concat) with validation accuracy 0.6186 and F1 0.6103, showing that combining RNA and image features with avgpool aggregation is promising. The main remaining uncertainty is whether the fusion strategy matters: concat may be sufficient, or weighted fusion may better balance the modalities. config_019 tests exactly that by changing only fusion from concat to weighted while keeping the best-known profile, aggregation, encoders, and model setting fixed. This is the most efficient next experiment because it exploits the current best direction, isolates one important design decision, and will guide whether future effort should focus on fusion tuning or stronger representations such as ViT or transformer aggregation."
}

